          "id": "step364_col1_half_level_initialization",
          "description": "cuinin on the chem170 single-column reference, step 364, TILE COLUMN 1 of 2 -- 12 LST, deep convection, and the step holding the COLDEST half level of the dumped set (184.8 K), so it reaches furthest into the pure-ice branch of the phase weight. Reference run: data/eqwefic/notes/chem170_scm_reference_run.md (em_scm_xy, Weisman-Klemp sounding over Kansas, 1997-06-20 12 UTC + 48 h, dx = 20 km, 59 levels, dt = 60 s, cu_physics = 16). Reference build: the real64 (kind_phys = real64) replay through kernels/ntiedtke_driver of WRF fork branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem170, with the seven constants cu_ntiedtke_init takes supplied at binary64 precision (they are ARGUMENTS); the scheme's own parameter block stays at its binary32 roundings, FORTRAN_BUGS N109. The values come from a stage dump taken immediately after the cuinin call, because every one of its outputs is a cumastrn local that the updraught and the rest overwrite before the routine returns. `qs_h` is asserted through `qs_h_defined`, which zeroes the top entry on both sides: cuinin never assigns `pqsenh(:,1)` even though the array is intent(out), so there is nothing there to match. Vertical ordering is the scheme's own TOP-DOWN kernel ordering, index 1 at the model top. Algebraic observeds at t = 0 with no ODE state, so the empty time_span is one static evaluation.",
